         Maximum number of iterations of every solve of a velocity update, of which a substep with contacts runs several,
         a safety limit for the environments whose solve does not reach its tolerance. Such an environment keeps its
         last iterate and reports the failure (see `ShellSolver.get_envs_solver_failure`). Defaults to 1000.
+    contact_pad_stiffness : float, optional
+        Compression-only physical pad stiffness per supplied projected reference area, in N/m^3. Paired with
+        contact_pad_geometry, this selects one material quadrature point per face with fixed physical compliance.
+        Its linear reference-geometry kinematics require elastic fixed topology and floating-point reductions.
+        Defaults to None, using the ordinary contact model.
+    contact_pad_geometry : str, optional
+        NPZ containing points_m, corners_m, jacobians and projected_area_m2 in built face order. Point coordinates
+        and face-corner coordinates are in the initial world frame, and the three displacement Jacobians per face
+        must reproduce infinitesimal rigid motions. The force transfer is their transpose. Defaults to None.
     fracture_capacity : float, optional
         Number of vertices a fracturable sheet can create by splitting, as a fraction of its own vertex count. Each one
         costs memory in every environment. Fracture stops in an environment that exhausted it. Defaults to 1.0.
